  "text": "Title: Reading Don Quixote\n\nAlexandra retired from the Mathematics Department at Northwestern at the age of sixty-one, \nrelatively early for an academic. When I asked why, she explained that living under a \ndictatorship had deprived her of so much—books, films, and experiences. Growing up, \nshe hadn’t even been familiar with the Bible. She arrived in the West with voracious \ncuriosity, determined to make up for the time lost. After earning her doctorate at Yale \nand holding positions at prestigious universities across the country, she retired from \nteaching not to rest, but to become a full-time student. \nReading Don Quixote was one of her learning projects.",
